{
  "id": "nema_insulation_classes",
  "title": "NEMA Insulation Classes",
  "description": "Electrical insulation systems rated by standard NEMA classifications to maximize allowable operating temperatures.",
  "type": "chart-table",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## NEMA Insulation Classes\n\nElectrical insulation systems are rated by standard NEMA (National Electrical Manufacturers Association) classifications according to maximum allowable operating temperature.\n\n### Key Information:\n- Reference ambient temperature: 40°C\n- Operating temperature = Reference temperature + Allowable temperature rise + Hot spot allowance (typically 10°C)\n- Each 10°C rise above rating may reduce motor lifetime by one half\n- Class B is most common for U.S. 60-cycle motors\n- Class F is most common for international and 50-cycle motors"
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Temperature Class",
        "Max Temp (°C)",
        "Max Temp (°F)",
        "Temp Rise @ 1.0 SF (°C)",
        "Temp Rise @ 1.15 SF (°C)"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "A",
          105,
          221,
          60,
          70
        ],
        [
          "B",
          130,
          266,
          80,
          90
        ],
        [
          "F",
          155,
          311,
          105,
          115
        ],
        [
          "H",
          180,
          356,
          125,
          "-"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "tempCelsius",
          "label": "Temperature (°C)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 40,
          "unit": "°C"
        },
        {
          "id": "tempRise",
          "label": "Allowable Temperature Rise (°C)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 105,
          "unit": "°C"
        },
        {
          "id": "hotSpot",
          "label": "Hot Spot Allowance (°C)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 10,
          "unit": "°C"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "operatingTempC",
          "label": "Operating Temperature",
          "formula": "inputs.tempCelsius + inputs.tempRise + inputs.hotSpot",
          "unit": "°C",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "operatingTempF",
          "label": "Operating Temperature",
          "formula": "(inputs.tempCelsius + inputs.tempRise + inputs.hotSpot) * 9 / 5 + 32",
          "unit": "°F",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chart",
      "content": "Motor Lifetime Comparison by Insulation Class",
      "options": {
        "title": {
          "text": "Estimated Motor Lifetime by Insulation Class (at 180°C)",
          "left": "center"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "trigger": "axis",
          "axisPointer": {
            "type": "shadow"
          }
        },
        "xAxis": {
          "type": "category",
          "data": [
            "Class A",
            "Class B",
            "Class F",
            "Class H"
          ]
        },
        "yAxis": {
          "type": "value",
          "name": "Lifetime (hours)",
          "scale": true
        },
        "series": [
          {
            "data": [
              300,
              1800,
              8500,
              50000
            ],
            "type": "bar",
            "itemStyle": {
              "color": "#1f77b4"
            }
          }
        ],
        "grid": {
          "left": "10%",
          "right": "10%",
          "bottom": "15%",
          "top": "15%",
          "containLabel": true
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}